  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Percentage of schools that integrate disaster and climate resilience measures</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2023-08-12" value="0" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-08-12"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2026-12-12"></period-end>
     <target value="80">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">In progress. 
In partnership with University of the Philippines National Engineering Centre, DepEd has developed a tool that identifies disaster resilience measures and helps to prioritize school infrastructure investments under the World Bank-financed Infrastructure for Safer and Resilient Schools Project (ISRS). This tool is being scaled up to cover all public schools in DepEd&apos;s National School Building Index database. 
 At the national planning level, the World Bank is promoting the use of the ISRS analysis to DepEd Education Facilities Division to update DepEd&apos;s current &#x201c;Rubric for New Construction&#x201d; used by DepEd for investment prioritization, to ensure that investments are risk-informed.

At the school level, the World Bank is working with DepEd Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Service and DOST to develop the PlanSmart for Safe Schools platform, which can provide useful information for schools.

Information source: DepEd</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Percentage of schools in the GMMA that implement risk-informed disaster and climate preparedness and response plans</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2023-08-12" value="0" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-08-12"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2026-12-12"></period-end>
     <target value="80">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">In progress. 

To meet the target of 80% of schools implementing emergency preparedness and response plans, DepEd is finalizing its School Contingency Planning guidebook, which is the basis for the PlanSmart for Safe Schools application under development. This tool, to be developed by DOST in partnership with DepEd, will help formulate risk-informed and evidence-based contingency plans in schools. DepEd is conducting server capacity improvement of the PlanSmart application, and DepEd committed to launch the app, finalize the DOST-DepEd Memorandum of Agreement, and   the vetting of the School Contingency Planning Guidebook in August 2025. Trainings will be conducted starting in the last quarter of 2025. Depending on the success of the platform, DepEd plans to scale up its use beyond the GMMA to include all schools nationwide.

Information source: DepEd</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of LGUs that have developed and integrated resilient urban design strategies in their land use plans (CLUPs).</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2023-08-12" value="0" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-08-12"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2026-12-12"></period-end>
     <target value="30">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">In progress.
This indicator refers to an updated CLUP and Zoning Ordinance that includes resilient urban design strategies, or local urban design guide presented at the Local Development Council (LDC). DHSUD, with support from the World Bank, developed its Resilient Urban Design Development (RUDD) Guidelines, which were approved in April 2025 under Department Circular No. 2025-005 Adopting the RUDD Guidelines for application in the CLUP and Zoning ordinance. Training of trainers on the use of the Guidelines was conducted from July 7 to 11, 2025. DHSUD has identified the 30 pilot LGUs that will be trained/assisted in the development and integration of RUDD into their CLUPs. The PlanSmart for Sustainable Human Settlements under development will integrate the urban design strategies in the CLUPs of LGUs.

Information source: DHSUD</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of LGUs that implement zoning regulations based on disaster and climate risk-informed CLUPs.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2023-08-12" value="0" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-08-12"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2026-12-12"></period-end>
     <target value="200">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Substantially achieved.

114 Local Government Units (LGUs) have disaster and climate risk-informed Comprehensive Land Use Plans (CLUP) and corresponding Zoning Ordinance. These LGUs utilized the digital templates for the Harmonized Ecological Profile (EP) with Climate and Disaster Risk Assessment (CDRA) and CLUP. These digital templates are bases for the PlanSmart for Sustainable Human Settlements web platform, under development by DOST. DHSUD is expected to exceed this target once LGUs can use the platform, as it will facilitate the seamless integration of risk information in LGU&apos;s land use planning. DHSUD, in partnership with DOST and with support from the World Bank, has completed the Harmonized EP with CDRA module of the PlanSmart system. Other activities to enable launching of the PlanSmart platform by October 2025 include: processing of data from LGUs; and Beta Testing of the application focused on CLUP module by September 2025.

Information source: DHSUD</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="114"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of LGUs that have developed plans for green and open spaces using DHSUD&apos;s guidelines</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2023-08-12" value="0" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-08-12"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2026-12-12"></period-end>
     <target value="30">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partially achieved.

This indicator measures the number of LGUs which submitted the plans which were assessed as compliant with the Guidelines and approved by DHSUD. DHSUD, with support from the World Bank, developed its Green and Open Spaces Development (GOSD) Guidelines. As of this mission, 50 LGUs have submitted GOSD plans, of which, 9 have been approved and 41 are currently under review by DHSUD to ensure compliance with the DHSUD Guidelines. The PlanSmart for Sustainable Human Settlements under development will integrate green and open spaces in the CLUPs of LGUs.

Information source: DHSUD</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="9"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Percentage of health facilities funded under the DOH Health Facilities Enhancement Program that integrate disaster and climate resilience measures</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2023-08-12" value="25" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-08-12"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2026-12-12"></period-end>
     <target value="95">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">In progress. Previous missions have agreed that this indicator will cover government hospitals that are: (i) licensed by DOH and funded through their HFEP for infrastructure; (ii) compliant with at least 76% (corresponding to a GVA 3-star rating) or at least a 1-star GVA rating but with  80 % rating on 3 of the 8 GVA criteria&#x2014;Environmentally Resilient Health Facility, Site Sustainability, and Materials Sustainability&#x2014;which are related to resilience; and (iii) excludes HFEP-funded purchase of equipment and motor vehicles. As of this Mission, DOH reported that 72% or 130 out of 181 government hospitals funded in 2024 and 2025 are deemed to have integrated resilience measures.
DOH and the World Bank agreed to revisit the methodology to ensure that the GVA criteria used are focused on disaster and climate resilience-related aspects. DOH will also designate the responsible office in the department for Cat DDO implementation, following their internal staffing changes.
Information source: DOH</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="25"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
